{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "15700464",
      "title": "Context API Summary (and why NOT to use it instead of Redux)",
      "sourceHash": "2419be6bc4b50e5a1459e96513a922226cd106ede9ab68a015f63836b2120a40",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.25,
          "end": 4.83,
          "en": "Well, one huge downside is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.83,
          "end": 8.67,
          "en": "this comment here by a React team member.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.67,
          "end": 12.48,
          "en": "The statement here is clear, the context is great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.48,
          "end": 17.11,
          "en": "for low-frequency updates but not for high-frequency ones.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.11,
          "end": 20.37,
          "en": "That means if you have something which changes rarely,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.37,
          "end": 22.84,
          "en": "let's say the user authentication status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.84,
          "end": 26.12,
          "en": "or just the example I used in the React Hooks module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.12,
          "end": 29.55,
          "en": "that is fine to be covered with the context API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.55,
          "end": 33.24,
          "en": "because this will not change all the time, not that often.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.24,
          "end": 35.28,
          "en": "The same would be the case if you have something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.28,
          "end": 37.68,
          "en": "like theme-ing on a page, or something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.68,
          "end": 40.07,
          "en": "which doesn't change all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.07,
          "end": 41.69,
          "en": "For a favorite status like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.69,
          "end": 43.08,
          "en": "you could already argue that it's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.08,
          "end": 45.11,
          "en": "quite a high-frequency update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.11,
          "end": 47.92,
          "en": "Now, obviously users might not be tapping these buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.92,
          "end": 51.07,
          "en": "every second but still switching the favorite status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.07,
          "end": 54.87,
          "en": "of something will very likely occur way more often",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.87,
          "end": 58.49,
          "en": "than logging in or changing the theme of a page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.49,
          "end": 60.53,
          "en": "and therefore I would argue that this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.53,
          "end": 62.47,
          "en": "is more on the high-frequency side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.47,
          "end": 64.77,
          "en": "just like maybe managing a shopping cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.77,
          "end": 68.62,
          "en": "Basically anything which changes rather often.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.62,
          "end": 72.11,
          "en": "The context API of course works in that case but",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.11,
          "end": 74.26,
          "en": "regarding the performance it's simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.26,
          "end": 76.32,
          "en": "not optimized for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.32,
          "end": 78.941,
          "en": "The way the react context API works is such that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.941,
          "end": 82.31,
          "en": "whenever something changes in your context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.31,
          "end": 85.94,
          "en": "it has no way of cleverly figuring out which component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.94,
          "end": 88.62,
          "en": "that uses this context really is concerned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.62,
          "end": 90.22,
          "en": "and which component is not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.22,
          "end": 94.31,
          "en": "Which means that every component that uses use context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.31,
          "end": 96.25,
          "en": "will rebuild, will re-render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.25,
          "end": 98.24000000000001,
          "en": "when you switch something in that context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.24000000000001,
          "end": 101.27000000000001,
          "en": "No matter if it's directly effected or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.27000000000001,
          "end": 103.59,
          "en": "And in general the react context API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 103.59,
          "end": 106.47999999999999,
          "en": "is simply not optimized and not meant to be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 106.47999999999999,
          "end": 109.89,
          "en": "your Global State Management tool in your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.89,
          "end": 113.47,
          "en": "It's meant for some states, like authentication status,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.47,
          "end": 116.09,
          "en": "like the theme but not for all your states",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.09,
          "end": 119.03999999999999,
          "en": "because of these missing optimizations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.03999999999999,
          "end": 123.153,
          "en": "and all of this missing intent behind the context API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.1,
          "end": 127.86,
          "en": "Hence it is great for some things like authentication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.86,
          "end": 129.56,
          "en": "which I mentioned a couple of times",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.56,
          "end": 132.97,
          "en": "but not for all use cases not for all scenarios",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132.97,
          "end": 135.79,
          "en": "and something like your products and the favorite status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.79,
          "end": 138.07,
          "en": "is probably not what you want to manage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.07,
          "end": 141.77,
          "en": "with the context API in larger projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.77,
          "end": 145.72,
          "en": "But there still is a non redux alternative for that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.72,
          "end": 147.893,
          "en": "and that's what we'll have a look at next.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}